// The sculptbrush package: Sculpt Mode's brushes and stroke engine, on a fixed-topology
// mesh.PolyMesh (density comes from sculpt's 'subdivide', multires or voxel remesh; there
// is no dynamic topology). A recipe is data, a list of 'Stroke's, and replaying it gives the
// same bits on every machine.
//
//   import sculptbrush use *;
//   mut sc = Sculptor.of(&mesh);                       // a working copy
//   mut pts = List[Vec3].empty();  pts.push(a);  pts.push(b);
//   mut st = Stroke.make(Brush.of(BrushClayStrips), pts, 0.2, 1.);   // brush, path, radius, strength
//   st.mirrorAcross(origin, normal);                   // symmetry
//   imm report = sc.stroke(&st);                       // dabs, vertices moved, needsDensity
//   imm sculpted = sc.finish();
//
// - 'Stroke' and 'Brush' (stroke.cone): a stroke is a brush, a path (points; methods StrokeSpace, StrokeDots,
//   StrokeAnchored, StrokeLine, StrokeCurve, as Blender's space, dots, anchored, line and curve), a radius,
//   a strength, curves of radius and of strength along the stroke (pressure: 'pressureCurve', 'rampCurve'),
//   a falloff across the dab (sculpt's 'Falloff', so all of Blender's brush curves and a custom one), the
//   inverted action ('subtract', Blender's Ctrl), mirror planes ('mirrorAcross'), a front-faces-only gate,
//   a face-set limit, the mask ("mask" channel, sculpt's), an alpha (a stamp, 'Alpha', 'alphaFrom'), and
//   whether the path is snapped to the surface. 'bezierPoints' and 'splinePoints' make paths.
// - 'Sculptor' (sculptor.cone): applies strokes in order; 'sculptStroke' and 'sculptStrokes' are the one-shot
//   forms; 'captureBase' is Blender's persistent base for Layer; 'StrokeReport' says when a stroke
//   stretched the surface thin ('needsDensity': subdivide or remesh before going on).
// - The brushes (kernels.cone), each a function of the dab to a displacement per vertex, as Blender's manual
//   describes it (names as Blender's, ZBrush's in brackets):
//     BrushDraw (Standard), BrushDrawSharp, BrushClay, BrushClayStrips (ClayBuildup), BrushLayer, BrushInflate
//     (Inflat), BrushBlob, BrushCrease, BrushDam (Dam Standard), BrushSmooth (Laplacian, with a Taubin step
//     back out), BrushPlane (Flatten, Fill, Scrape presets; Flatten inverted is Contrast; ZBrush Flatten and
//     hPolish), BrushPinch (inverted: Magnify), BrushGrab (Move), BrushElastic (Elastic Deform: regularised
//     biscale Kelvinlets), BrushSnakeHook (fixed topology), BrushThumb, BrushNudge, BrushRotate, BrushSlideRelax
//     (Relax Slide), BrushPose (a segment turned about a pivot found automatically), BrushMask (paints the
//     mask; subtract erases), BrushMoveTopological (ZBrush Move Topological: grab with weights by distance
//     along the surface).
// - Strokes in a shape's own coordinates (anatomy.cone): 'anatomyPoint' and 'anatomyHit' map (limb, along,
//   around) of skinmesh's channels to a surface point; 'anatomyPath', 'alongPlaces', 'aroundPlaces' make a
//   stroke's points from them, so the same recipe lands on the same anatomy when proportions change.
//
// Method choices worth knowing (each stated where it is made):
// - The dab centre is snapped by the tangent plane at the nearest vertex (a hash over the stroke's start
//   positions), not by a tree over the triangles, because a recipe of 200 strokes cannot afford a tree
//   rebuilt after each one; and each dab lifts its centre by how far the vertex under it has moved since
//   the stroke began, so a stroke goes on working on the surface it makes.
// - Brushes follow Blender's manual for what they do; the amounts (how high a stroke builds) are tuned here,
//   not taken from its source. Rotate's angle is given as tan(half angle) and Pose's turn is a normalised
//   quaternion lerp, so that no kernel calls a trigonometric function: the only libm call in a stroke is
//   what a falloff makes (FalloffGauss uses exp: avoid it in a recipe that must be exact).
// - Layer without 'captureBase' raises from where each stroke began; with it, from the captured surface.
//
// Not built: dynamic topology (Snake Hook, Grab and Thumb stretch a fixed mesh: see 'needsDensity'),
// radial symmetry, view-dependent gates (front faces are by the dab's normal, not a camera), Boundary,
// Cloth, Multiplane Scrape, Elastic Snake Hook, scale and twist Kelvinlets.
//
// The algorithms are from the literature; parameters follow Blender's manual, never its source:
// - regularised Kelvinlets: de Goes and James, "Regularized Kelvinlets: sculpting brushes based on
//   fundamental solutions of elasticity", ACM Transactions on Graphics 36(4), 2017, and their biscale form;
// - the fast-marching surface distance Pose and Move Topological use is sculpt's (select.cone).
//
// Files (one module; only this root imports):
//
//   stroke.cone     Brush, Alpha, SymPlane, Stroke, the curves, paths and dab spacing
//   sculptor.cone   Sculptor: strokes to dabs, gathering a dab's vertices and their weights, the gates,
//                   symmetry, grab and pose, the report
//   kernels.cone    each brush's displacement, the relax step, the Kelvinlets
//   anatomy.cone    strokes in (limb, along, around)

mod sculptbrush;

import libc;
import geomath use *;
import collections use *;
import mesh use *;
import sculpt use *;
